Buspirone hydrochloride tablets in measured doses, put up for retail sale, fall under heading 3004 as medicaments. Buspirone's structure contains a pyrimidine ring (2-pyrimidinyl piperazine) and an azaspirodecanedione. Within 3004.90, the specific "other" subheadings are 3004.90.92 (other) and 3004.90.91 (a "Other" subdivision). Buspirone is not an antibiotic, hormone, or alkaloid, so it goes to 3004.90.

Since the tablets are finished dosage forms, 3004.90.9290 is a plausible code. In the HTSUS, 3004.90.92 is "Other" and the statistical suffix 90 is "Other". I recall CBP rulings on buspirone classifying it in 3004.90.9290, so I'll go with that.

{"hts_code": "3004.90.9290", "reason": "Buspirone hydrochloride tablets are finished medicaments in measured doses for retail sale, which fall under heading 3004 and, as a non-specified anxiolytic, under the residual subheading 3004.90.92."}
